    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66678" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταΐσσω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rush after, rush upon</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, always in pres. or aor.
			part. with another Verb, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κτεῖνε μεταΐσσων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.398
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠὲ μεταΐξας . . ἕλοιτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.236
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.564
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠὲ μεταΐξας θάνατον τεύξειεν ἑκάστῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					20.11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τινά</span>
			<i>follow closely in</i> another's <i>steps</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				5.43
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>]</div>
